cdn.realtor.ca/listing/TS639268825120830000/reb10/highres/6/E4511876_40.jpg","https://ddfcdn.realtor.ca/listing/TS639268825120830000/reb10/highres/6/E4511876_41.jpg"],"remarks":"For a moment, you could forget you’re in Edmonton. There’s something distinctly New York about this place, not the polished version, but the old buildings tucked between newer ones, where the history is still very much part of the address. The McLeod Building has stood downtown since 1915, once holding the title of Edmonton’s tallest building and remaining one of the city’s most recognizable pieces of architecture. More than a century later, much of what made it remarkable is still here. And somewhere above the marble lobby is this: an unexpectedly open, light-filled loft that feels slightly out of place in the best way. It’s unconventional, full of character and difficult to compare to much else in the city. A home for someone who would rather have something interesting than something new. Because Edmonton has newer buildings, taller buildings and certainly more modern buildings. But there is only one McLeod. Tastefully renovated, move in ready & a reservation waiting for you downstairs at Woodwork. (id:67522)","facts":[["Price","$224,900"],["Type","Condo"],["Bedrooms","1"],["Bathrooms","1"],["Living area","538 sq ft"],["Lot size","120 sq ft"],["Year built","1905"],["Condo fee","$629 monthly"],["Neighbourhood","Downtown"],["Town","Edmonton"],["Postal code","T6J0N8"],["MLS® number","E4511876"],["Listed","October 6, 2026"]],"features":[["Appliances","Refrigerator, Dishwasher, Stove, Hood Fan, Washer/Dryer Combo, Window Coverings"],["Heating","Hot water radiator heat"],["Condo fee includes","Property Management, Caretaker, Heat, Electricity, Water, Insurance, Other, See Remarks"]],"rooms":[["Living room","Main level","4.87 m × 3.26 m (16'0\" × 10'8\")"],["Kitchen","Main level","5.18 m × 3.28 m (17'0\" × 10'9\")"],["Primary Bedroom","Main level","2.82 m × 4.00 m (9'3\" × 13'1\")"]],"courtesy":"